  <!-- ====================================================
    SECTION 2 — COMPANY STORY
  ==================================================== -->
  <section class="sec" aria-labelledby="story-h2">
    <div class="c">
      <span class="eye">Our Story</span>
      <h2 class="h2" id="story-h2">From 25 Machines to a Full-Package Apparel Manufacturer — Dhaka, 1998 to Now</h2>
      <div class="g2" style="margin-top:1.5rem;">
        <div>
          <p class="body">SDF Clothing started on August 22, 1998 — twenty-five sewing machines, a modest space in Dhaka's textile district, and a single conviction: that a Bangladesh apparel factory could compete on quality, transparency, and reliability, not just price. Chowdhury Remon, who founded the company, had spent years working in the garment industry before deciding that the right approach was to build a factory that served international brands directly — no buying house layer, no agent commission, no opacity between the brand and where its clothes were made.</p>
          <p class="body">The first EU export client arrived in 2003. ISO 9001 quality certification came in 2011. GOTS organic certification and OEKO-TEX Standard 100 followed in 2017, driven by EU market demand from the brands we were already supplying. BSCI and SEDEX SMETA social compliance certification was added in 2019. By 2021, the factory had expanded to its current 75,000 sq ft facility with dedicated production lines for knitwear, woven apparel, and outerwear.</p>
          <p class="body">Today SDF Clothing is a full-package apparel manufacturer serving 200+ brands across 36 countries. Full-package means exactly what it says: we source fabric, develop patterns, produce samples, run bulk production, apply branding and embroidery, conduct AQL 2.5 inspection, pack, and arrange FOB shipment from Chittagong port. The brand sends a tech pack. We send finished, certified, compliant apparel ready for retail.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="card" style="margin-bottom:1.2rem;">
            <div class="h3">What "Full-Package Apparel Manufacturer" Actually Means</div>
            <p class="body" style="margin-bottom:0.6rem;">There is a meaningful difference between a CMT factory (which cuts, makes, and trims from fabric you supply) and a full-package apparel manufacturer (which handles the complete supply chain). At SDF Clothing, full-package means:</p>
            <ul class="cl green">
              <li>Fabric sourcing from our vetted GOTS, OEKO-TEX, and GRS certified mills</li>
              <li>Pattern making, grading, and size spec development</li>
              <li>Proto and pre-production sampling — 14-day turnaround</li>
              <li>Bulk production with in-line QC at every stage</li>
              <li>Embroidery, screen printing, DTF, sublimation in-house</li>
              <li>AQL 2.5 final inspection before shipment approval</li>
              <li>Complete compliance documentation and FOB shipping</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="card">
            <div class="h3">Production Models</div>
            <ul class="cl">
              <li><strong style="color:#e0e0e0;">OEM</strong> — Original Equipment Manufacturing from your tech pack and specifications</li>
              <li><strong style="color:#e0e0e0;">Private Label</strong> — Full branding, labelling, and packaging under your brand identity</li>
              <li><strong style="color:#e0e0e0;">CMT</strong> — Cut, Make, Trim from your supplied fabric and trims</li>
              <li><strong style="color:#e0e0e0;">ODM</strong> — Our design development adapted to your target market and buyer</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

