  ==================================================== -->
  <section class="sec" aria-labelledby="faq-h2">
    <div class="c">
      <span class="eye">Common Questions</span>
      <h2 class="h2" id="faq-h2">Questions Buyers Ask About SDF Clothing</h2>
      <p class="lead">Click any question to expand the answer.</p>

      <div class="faq-wrap" id="faq-wrap">

        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-a1">
            <span class="faq-q">What is the minimum order quantity for apparel production?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-body" id="faq-a1" role="region">
            <p class="faq-a"><strong>300 pieces per style</strong> — across OEM, private label, CMT, and ODM. Size distribution within the 300 pieces is fully flexible. Multiple styles on the same purchase order each carry their own 300-piece minimum. A startup brand ordering two styles at 300 pieces each (600 total) is a standard first order — no higher MOQ for new clients, no trial order surcharges.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-a2">
            <span class="faq-q">How does SDF Clothing differ from other apparel manufacturers in Bangladesh?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-body" id="faq-a2" role="region">
            <p class="faq-a">Three things most clients mention: <strong>300-piece MOQ</strong> — most Bangladesh apparel factories start at 500–1,000 pieces per style. <strong>Full-chain GOTS certification</strong> — many factories claim to use organic cotton but cannot issue a GOTS certificate of conformity for your organic labelling claim. We can, because our certification covers every stage from fibre to finished apparel. <strong>EU EPR 2026 readiness</strong> — we generate Digital Product Passport data files as standard for EU orders. Most Bangladesh apparel manufacturers are not doing this yet. Beyond those, direct factory access means pricing transparency that a buying house or agent cannot offer.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-a3">
            <span class="faq-q">What is the production lead time from brief to shipment?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-body" id="faq-a3" role="region">
            <p class="faq-a">Proto sample: <strong>14 days</strong> from confirmed brief, DHL Express to your door. Pre-production sample: 10 days after proto approval. Bulk production: <strong>30–45 days</strong> from PP sample sign-off. Total first-order time from brief to FOB Chittagong: 55–65 days. Repeat orders run faster — fabric and PP approval already in place. Ocean freight to EU ports (Rotterdam, Hamburg, Genova): 22–28 additional transit days. Air freight to major EU/UK airports: 4–5 days.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-a4">
            <span class="faq-q">Do EU and UK brands pay import duty on apparel from SDF Clothing?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-body" id="faq-a4" role="region">
            <p class="faq-a"><strong>No.</strong> Bangladesh holds EU GSP EBA (Everything But Arms) status — 0% import duty on most apparel (HS chapters 61 and 62) into all 27 EU member states and the UK under the UK GSP scheme. Standard EU MFN duty on clothing is 12% of CIF value — on a €100,000 order that is €12,000 saved versus sourcing from China or other non-GSP countries. We prepare EUR.1 Movement Certificates for every EU and UK shipment. See our <a href="/clothing-manufacturer-italy">Italy page</a>, <a href="/clothing-manufacturer-germany">Germany page</a>, or <a href="/clothing-manufacturer-uk">UK page</a> for country-specific duty and customs detail.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-a5">
            <span class="faq-q">Can SDF Clothing produce GOTS certified organic apparel?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-body" id="faq-a5" role="region">
            <p class="faq-a">Yes — and the distinction matters. We hold <strong>full-chain GOTS certification</strong>: from raw organic cotton sourcing through spinning, dyeing, cutting, sewing, and finishing at our Dhaka factory. Transaction certificates are issued at each stage. The GOTS certificate of conformity we provide with your order is the legal document that authorises your organic labelling claim in EU, UK, and USA markets. A factory that uses organic cotton but lacks GOTS scope certification cannot issue this — you cannot legally label the garments as organic without it.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-a6">
            <span class="faq-q">Does SDF Clothing work with startup fashion brands?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-body" id="faq-a6" role="region">
            <p class="faq-a">Yes. The 300-piece MOQ exists specifically because smaller brands deserve direct factory access too. A founder placing a debut collection at 300 pieces per style gets the same factory, the same certifications, the same quality control process, and the same compliance documentation as a brand ordering 50,000 pieces. Price per piece differs with volume — the production standard does not. We have worked with brands from their first-ever order through to large repeat accounts. Both are important to us.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-a7">
            <span class="faq-q">Can I visit the SDF Clothing factory in Bangladesh?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-body" id="faq-a7" role="region">
            <p class="faq-a">Yes. Factory visits are welcome for verified business partners — we encourage them. Third-party social and environmental audits at our facility are fully supported: SGS, Bureau Veritas, and Intertek all conduct audits here. If your retail buyer requires a specific audit format, we work with you to schedule it. We have nothing to hide. Factory transparency is a basic expectation of doing business with international brands, not a favour we grant selectively.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

